{"name":"Yours Truly","hex":"#fbd9cd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yours truly","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Used to close a note or letter."]},{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["I, me, or myself."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yours_truly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valediction","blocks":[{"text":"A valediction, parting phrase, or complimentary close in American English, is an expression used to say farewell, especially a word or phrase used to end a letter or message, or a speech made at a farewell."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valediction"},{"title":"Yours Truly (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Yours Truly are an Australian pop-punk band formed in 2016 in Sydney, New South Wales. Their debut studio album, Self Care (2020), peaked at number 19 on the ARIA Albums Chart."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yours_Truly_(band)"},{"title":"Yours Truly (Ariana Grande album)","blocks":[{"text":"Yours Truly is the debut studio album by American singer-songwriter Ariana Grande. It was released on August 30, 2013, by Republic Records. The album's songs were recorded over nearly a two-year period, with Harmony Samuels, Kenneth \"Babyface\" Edmonds, Patrick \"J. Que\" Smith and Grande's Victorious co-star Leon Thomas III, as well as others, handling the album's music production. Featured collaborators include Big Sean, Mika, Mac Miller, and The Wanted's Nathan Sykes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cb/Ariana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yours_Truly_(Ariana_Grande_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fc/Ariana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly_%28Tenth_Anniversary%29.png/250px-Ariana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly_%28Tenth_Anniversary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Ariana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly_%28Tenth_Anniversary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fc/Ariana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly_%28Tenth_Anniversary%29.png/250px-Ariana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly_%28Tenth_Anniversary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAriana_Grande_-_Yours_Truly_(Tenth_Anniversary).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Dirty_Picture_-_Get_Sleazy_Tour.jpg/500px-Dirty_Picture_-_Get_Sleazy_Tour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Dirty_Picture_-_Get_Sleazy_Tour.jpg/500px-Dirty_Picture_-_Get_Sleazy_Tour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grande became the fifteenth female artist overall to have her debut album top the US Billboard 200 albums chart and the first since Kesha's Animal in 2010.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADirty_Picture_-_Get_Sleazy_Tour.jpg"}],"sounds":{"yours truly":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/En-us-yours_truly.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/En-us-yours_truly.ogg/En-us-yours_truly.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/En-au-yours_truly.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/82/En-au-yours_truly.ogg/En-au-yours_truly.ogg.mp3"}]}}}